7. Phase 6 notes
Two checks: Missing Impact/Likelihood after 14 days, and Not Reviewed in 90 Days. Both read saved filters from the Risk & Opportunities Audit Dashboard. The filter ids stay in local settings only.
Both checks send email to the owner (the assignee, else the reporter). A ticket with no owner goes on an exception list to the Odd Squad. Nothing is written on any risk ticket, and no owner is mentioned (Eric, 2026-11-10).
Status and record comments go on the monthly audit ticket. US reads PS and PSC. NULSC reads PS only, after written authorization.
The planning estimate is higher than the ticket because the notifier and sent record must change from one message per kind per run date to one email per owner with a record per key. Without it, a retry after a partial failure would resend emails.
The ticket describes a weekly report with a 52-hour saving. The report owner runs it monthly. Eric has not yet ruled on the saving, so treat 52 hours as unconfirmed.
Still open: the 14-day email subject, greeting and signer, one email per ticket or per owner, whether she wants a Confluence page, and the time per month today.
8. Code base and model use
AUTO-188 stays in the existing repo. Each phase is a new module or report inside adherence/, with tests and settings. Exceptions: Phase 8 (the viewer) may be a separate project, and Phase 4 may need its own runtime, depending on the hosting decision. Neither is in the six-month plan.
AUTO-56 is a new project, separate from this repo. The ticket does not fix a language. The proposal is a Python harness that does the deterministic work (Jira, GitLab, status triggers, logging, guardrails, tests) and calls a model API only where judgment is needed (identifying the manual location, writing the draft). Reusable gate pieces (Jira client, TOML settings, secret store, comments-only logging, "unavailable, never zero", network-blocked tests) would be copied and adapted.
Why the API and not skills: the harness controls exactly which fields are sent, which model each step uses, and the cost. The model is a setting. Guardrails (never touch source tickets, never write to a default or publishing branch, never invent a location) stay in code. Tests use a fake model client.
Model use in the plan: none in the AUTO-188 phases in the plan. AUTO-56 Phases 0, 1 and 3 use a model. The only AUTO-188 phase that uses one is Phase 5, which is not in the plan.
Security: sending content through the API and through skills carries the same data question. The API gives more control and a clearer answer to "what leaves the building".
